From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] buffer_cache: EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=4 checks native banks per page on every bind,
 EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS=1 logs pages that changed while the tracker had them clean

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series), off unless EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=4 or
EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS=1 is set. Port of the bank part of Lichii PR 345, a1b555012a (celmax85), which
replaces Eglantine 031e07436c (kraibse), our EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=2.

T42 uploads a 64 KiB native bank once per frame per address. kraibse measured one material pure
white for one or two frames, 1 in 500 to 1 in 690 presents with a still camera, and none in 1000
with an upload on every bind. Mode 2 here marks all 16 pages on every bind, which costs two mprotect
calls per page and a 64 KiB upload. Mode 4 compares each page with a snapshot of its last contents
on every bind and marks only the pages that changed, so an unchanged bank costs a memcmp.

Changes from a1b555012a: a mode of the existing switch, not the new default. Snapshots are capped by
EDEN_NX2_BANK_PAGES (4096 pages, 16 MiB; Lichii 16384, 64 MiB, too much for our pool). The compare
in place is our EDEN_NX2_UBO_INPLACE already. Its memory.cpp counters, gpu.cpp and rasterizer
batching are speed or debug work with no link to the flashes and are left out.

EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS=1 needs no mode and only looks in modes 0 to 3. It logs "Native bank pages
checked" every 2^18 pages, with the total of changed pages the tracker had clean, and up to 50 lines
per 10 s "Native bank page ... changed unseen" with the first changed word. Unseen means the page's
bytes changed, the tracker has it clean and no tracked CPU write landed in its 4 MiB since the last
check. So the tracker did not know yet, which is not proof of a lost write: a GPU write can wait in
dirty memory until the next InvalidateGPUCache. Those log times can be set against the flash times.

Use it with EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT=1. T42's once per frame mark moves the write epoch of the whole
4 MiB before a bank's next check, so without that switch unseen stays 0 whatever happens, and a
warning says so. A bank sharing its 4 MiB with busy data can still hide changes, so 0 unseen proves
nothing: read the "tracker clean" total too. With that switch uploads are direct, which is not quite
T42, and the check adds a 64 KiB compare per bind on the GPU thread. This bug is sensitive to timing,
so check that the run still flashes. If "Native bank snapshots forgotten" shows up, the cap was hit
and every page counts as new, so mode 4 then acts like mode 2.

On T42 mode 2 lowered the flashes but did not end them: run177 15 at the Lost Woods doorway against
40 and 54 in two base runs, same fps, standing still, one run. EDEN_NX2_FENCE_FLUSH_US=0 did better
(run178 and run179: 0). Mode 2 does several things at once: fresher bytes, more uploads, some of them
with barriers and a render pass end, and a moved epoch. So mode 2 against mode 4 does not single one
out. Unset, nothing changes. Not built, not run.
---
 .../video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h    | 143 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h          |  10 ++
 2 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 74d02bd..e3300de 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -1514,16 +1514,29 @@ void BufferCache<P>::BindHostGraphicsUniformBuffer(size_t stage, u32 index, u32
     // (Splatoon Raiders: the dialogue box corners in c1). Writes to that memory can go unnoticed by
     // the memory tracker, leaving stale host contents, so upload such a bank again once per frame.
     // EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD: 0 off, 1 once per frame (unset), 2 every bind of a 64 KiB bank, 3 every
-    // bind of any native bank. Once per frame left Ocarina of Time's per-draw material data stale
-    // for a frame now and then (white flashes); every bind costs front-thread time.
+    // bind of any native bank, 4 every bind of a 64 KiB bank, but only the pages whose bytes changed
+    // since the last check (Nx2CheckBankPages). Once per frame left Ocarina of Time's per-draw
+    // material data stale for a frame now and then (white flashes); every bind costs front-thread
+    // time.
     static const char bank_mode = [] {
         const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD");
         return value != nullptr ? value[0] : '1';
     }();
+    // EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS=1: count and log what the page check finds, whatever the mode. With modes
+    // 0 to 3 it only looks: nothing is marked, so the picture stays as it was. "Unseen" needs
+    // EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT=1, see Nx2CheckBankPages.
+    static const bool bank_stats = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] != '0';
+    }();
     const bool native_bank = has_host_buffer && size != 0 && gpu_memory != nullptr &&
                              gpu_memory->UsesNativeTiling() &&
                              !memory_tracker.IsRegionGpuModified(device_addr, size);
-    if (bank_mode != '0' && native_bank &&
+    if ((bank_mode == '4' || bank_stats) && native_bank &&
+        (*channel_state->uniform_buffer_sizes)[stage][index] == 0x10000) {
+        Nx2CheckBankPages(device_addr, size, bank_mode == '4', bank_stats);
+    }
+    if (bank_mode != '0' && bank_mode != '4' && native_bank &&
         (bank_mode == '3' || (*channel_state->uniform_buffer_sizes)[stage][index] == 0x10000) &&
         (bank_mode == '2' || bank_mode == '3' ||
          native_indirect_uniforms_this_frame.insert(device_addr).second)) {
@@ -1622,6 +1635,130 @@ void BufferCache<P>::BindHostGraphicsUniformBuffer(size_t stage, u32 index, u32
     channel_state->fast_bound_uniform_buffers[stage] &= ~(1u << binding_index);
 }
 
+template <class P>
+void BufferCache<P>::Nx2CheckBankPages(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool mark, bool stats) {
+    // The bank size is only an upper limit: stop at the end of the mapped memory.
+    u64 mapped_size = 0;
+    while (mapped_size < size &&
+           device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(device_addr + mapped_size) != nullptr) {
+        mapped_size += Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE - ((device_addr + mapped_size) & Core::DEVICE_PAGEMASK);
+    }
+    const u64 check_size = (std::min<u64>)(mapped_size, size);
+    if (check_size == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (stats) {
+        // A mark moves the write epoch of its whole 4 MiB, and modes 1 to 3 mark before a bank's
+        // next check, so that check always sees a moved epoch and "unseen" stays 0.
+        [[maybe_unused]] static const bool warned = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT");
+            if (value == nullptr || value[0] != '1') {
+                LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS: without EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT=1 bank "
+                                    "marks move the write epoch, so unseen stays 0");
+            }
+            return true;
+        }();
+    }
+    // EDEN_NX2_BANK_PAGES=<pages>: snapshots kept, 4 KiB each (unset: 4096, 16 MiB). Forgetting them
+    // makes every page new, so it marks and uploads them all once. Lichii keeps 16384 (64 MiB).
+    static const size_t max_pages = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BANK_PAGES");
+        const size_t pages = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+        return pages != 0 ? pages : size_t{4096};
+    }();
+    if (native_indirect_page_snapshots.size() >= max_pages) {
+        static u64 clears{};
+        if (++clears % 64 == 1) {
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Native bank snapshots forgotten at {} pages ({} times)", max_pages,
+                     clears);
+        }
+        native_indirect_page_snapshots.clear();
+    }
+    const DAddr first_page = Common::AlignDown(device_addr, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+    const DAddr end = device_addr + check_size;
+    for (DAddr page = first_page; page < end; page += Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE) {
+        const u8* const guest = device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(page);
+        if (guest == nullptr) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        auto [it, inserted] = native_indirect_page_snapshots.try_emplace(page);
+        Nx2BankPage& snapshot = it->second;
+        const bool same =
+            !inserted && std::memcmp(snapshot.bytes.data(), guest, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE) == 0;
+        if (stats) {
+            static std::array<u64, 3> counts{};
+            static std::array<u64, 4> changed_state{};
+            static u64 unseen{};
+            static u32 unseen_lines{};
+            static auto unseen_window = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+            ++counts[same ? 0 : (inserted ? 1 : 2)];
+            if (!same && !inserted) {
+                const bool known = memory_tracker.IsRegionCpuModified(page, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+                const bool gpu = memory_tracker.IsRegionGpuModified(page, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+                ++changed_state[(known ? 1 : 0) | (gpu ? 2 : 0)];
+                // Nothing marks the page and no tracked CPU write landed in its 4 MiB since the
+                // last check, so the tracker did not know of this change yet. That is not proof of
+                // a lost write: a GPU write can wait in dirty memory until the next
+                // InvalidateGPUCache, and a query report is copied straight into guest memory. A
+                // clean page with a moved epoch may have been uploaded by another binding: such
+                // pages only count in "tracker clean".
+                const bool unseen_change =
+                    !known && !gpu &&
+                    snapshot.epoch == memory_tracker.CpuWriteEpoch(page, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+                if (unseen_change) {
+                    ++unseen;
+                    // At most 50 lines in 10 s, so that loading cannot use them all up before the
+                    // scene under test.
+                    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+                    if (now - unseen_window >= std::chrono::seconds{10}) {
+                        unseen_window = now;
+                        unseen_lines = 0;
+                    }
+                }
+                if (unseen_change && unseen_lines < 50) {
+                    ++unseen_lines;
+                    u32 words = 0;
+                    u32 first = 0;
+                    u32 before = 0;
+                    u32 after = 0;
+                    for (u32 offset = 0; offset < Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE; offset += sizeof(u32)) {
+                        u32 old_word;
+                        u32 new_word;
+                        std::memcpy(&old_word, snapshot.bytes.data() + offset, sizeof(u32));
+                        std::memcpy(&new_word, guest + offset, sizeof(u32));
+                        if (old_word != new_word && words++ == 0) {
+                            first = offset;
+                            before = old_word;
+                            after = new_word;
+                        }
+                    }
+                    LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                             "Native bank page {:#x} of bank {:#x} changed unseen: {} words, first "
+                             "+{:#x} {:#010x} -> {:#010x}",
+                             page, device_addr, words, first, before, after);
+                }
+            }
+            if (((counts[0] + counts[1] + counts[2]) & 0x3ffff) == 0) {
+                LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                         "Native bank pages checked: same {}, new {}, changed {} (tracker clean "
+                         "{}, CPU-modified {}, GPU {}, both {}), {} unseen, {} kept",
+                         counts[0], counts[1], counts[2], changed_state[0], changed_state[1],
+                         changed_state[2], changed_state[3], unseen,
+                         native_indirect_page_snapshots.size());
+            }
+        }
+        if (!same) {
+            std::memcpy(snapshot.bytes.data(), guest, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+            if (mark) {
+                memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsCpuModified(page, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+            }
+        }
+        if (stats) {
+            snapshot.epoch = memory_tracker.CpuWriteEpoch(page, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 template <class P>
 void BufferCache<P>::ResolveMultiRangeStorage(Binding& binding, bool is_written,
                                               std::vector<MultiRangeSegment>& pool) {
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
index 8796914..2c68c19 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache_base.h
@@ -419,6 +419,16 @@ public:
     bool any_buffer_uploaded = false;
     /// Indirectly read banks of native programs already uploaded this frame.
     std::unordered_set<DAddr> native_indirect_uniforms_this_frame;
+    /// A page of a native program's indirectly read bank when last checked: unchanged pages keep
+    /// their tracking (marking one costs two mprotect calls).
+    struct Nx2BankPage {
+        std::array<u8, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE> bytes{};
+        u64 epoch{};
+    };
+    std::unordered_map<DAddr, Nx2BankPage> native_indirect_page_snapshots;
+    /// Compares each page of a bank with its snapshot (EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=4 marks the ones
+    /// that changed as CPU modified, EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS=1 logs what it finds).
+    void Nx2CheckBankPages(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool mark, bool stats);
 
     /// EDEN_NX2_DRAW_TUNING=0 turns off the two per-draw shortcuts below.
     static bool Nx2DrawTuning() {
